11.0.0 — the Sky's camera follows the dark smoothly; a chosen city stays; Cycle Tones tune a song to a cycle of the sky

New since 10078, built by the Echoel Studio run; nothing here is device-verified yet.
- Sky, camera picture (while the phone steers): near the limit of automatic exposure in the dark,
  the exposure goes on from where it stood, at most half again every half second, time before
  gain, instead of jumping to the longest time at the highest gain. Automatic returns when the
  light is back or after two overexposed frames in a row; focus holds meanwhile.
- Sky, place menu (top left): a chosen city stays when your location arrives later and when the Sky
  opens again; the first item goes back: "Here" (location off: "Last Known Place", once a place was
  found before).
- Sky, Cycle Tones (the list key, top right): 74 cycles of the Earth, the Moon, planets, minor
  planets and moons, each as a tone (one over its period, raised by octaves into octave 3), a tempo
  seven octaves lower and the concert pitch that puts the tone on its key. A row's tuning fork sets
  the song's key, concert pitch or tempo, or all three as one Undo; a tempo set by Flow, a MIDI clock
  or a jam stays. Under the ring the Sun, the Moon and a planet show their tone. Method after Hans
  Cousto; a calculation that claims nothing about what a tone does to a listener.
Limits, new: the key choice sets the song's root; in a new song (no scale, twelve equal steps) only
a Harmonizer that follows the key makes it heard. After dark the camera brightens step by step, at
most one step every half second. The lines under the ring stop growing at the bars' text size.
Older limits as in 10078.

Previous: 10078. A green commit that changes this file uploads build 10000 + run number. A test
list, not a source for claims (ContentPipeline/CLAIMS.md).

Five checks, yes or no. 1 and 2: one song with a synth track (Init or Warm Pad, Arpeggiator off)
holding long notes, and an audio track with a loop; 1 first.
1. Click off, Loop on, Play. Mixer → audio track's Effects → Add Effect → Tape; when "Loading…"
   is gone, tap On (it reads Off), tap again, then … › Remove. Each of the four times, no click or
   gap in the loop or the long notes? (A 5 ms dip or doubled beat is the glide.)
2. Tape removed; Stop. Arrange: hold the audio track's name › Automate › Volume, tap the lane halfway down
   at the song's end; hold the name again › Modulate › Pan › "Bar LFO → …". Press Play and let the
   loop come round twice; hold a screen key the clip never plays across the loop's end, let go; drag
   the synth's fader; tap the ruler at another bar. Stop, tap the ruler over the middle of the audio
   loop, Play. No click anywhere, and does the held key sound through the loop's end? (A clip note
   begun before a ruler tap is not picked up: not a no.)
3. Arm the audio track (its record key in Tracks), Record, a few seconds, Record again; wait until
   the take shows in Arrange; rename the song (Song menu → Song Settings…, a name no other song has,
   Done). Swipe the app away, open it, press Play, look under Song menu → Open: same song, new name,
   take playing, listed once? Then swipe it away, open it, swipe it away again within two seconds of
   the song showing, and open it once more: same song, no "did not finish starting" line?
4. Delay on a track, Time 500 (and a preset on another maker's plug-in, if any). Open another song
   (none: Song menu → New Song → Empty) and this one again; Delay's Ping-Pong On; swipe the app
   away, open it. Both times the values and the preset kept?
5. iPad, full screen, rotation lock off: one thing in each bottom-bar view (a key; Add Track ›
   Audio; ruler near bar 3; Add Scene; Master fader; Field full screen and back; Sky: a city, then
   Cycle Tones open and closed). Turn it once. Every view works, city still chosen, nothing
   overlapping either way? (Sideways the Sky is drawn on its side until dragged.) No iPad: "no iPad".
